※ pl4g-test: compile=ok opt=0,1
※ pl4g-test: run=native,qemu exit=1
※ pl4g-test: diag=none

※ Parentheses say how the operators group and mean nothing else.  The same
※ symbols without them are 1 | (6 ^ (3 & 2)), which is 5; with them they are
※ 1 | ((6 ^ 3) & 2), which is 1.
@[startup]
fn main() → u6:
    1u6 | (6u6 ^ 3u6) & 2u6
